/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A closure that gathers rows into a captured series is handed to a function, inside a rabbit, with the series outside it.

    A function handed to another is judged where it is handed over, as though it were cast there on
    anything the receiver is given or makes. The same hand-over outside the rabbit is accepted. (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Bind void to visit, given (the series of series of number rows, the void function work given (the series of number)):
    For each row in rows, repeat:
        Cast work on (row).
    Done.
Done.
Define rows as a series of series of number.
Insert (a series of number with (1, 2)) into rows.
Define collected as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Cast visit on (rows, a function given (the series of number row):
        Insert row into collected.
    Done).
Done.
State collected.
